/-!
# Explicit witnesses for mixed-form linear membership

Use the unchanged ATLAS column basis and the adapted coordinates (I,H,U)
from ../source/README.md. The twelve columns H complement I inside ker(A-1).
The forty displayed 12 by 50 matrices are the proposed mixed-evaluation
space. Definitions alone assert neither spanning nor a restriction on g.
The pairing inverse is certified in Coordinates.lean.

The finite obligations are:
* the image of the radical-I forms under Hᵀ R L is exactly mixedSpace;
* Hᵀ R factors through C(A-1) for every radical-I form;
* the right-stabilizer and its J-adjoint, with the reconstructed base column,
  lie in the published 125-generator restrictionLinearSpace.

The source arrays are generated by source/generate_data.py from the retained
untrusted calculations. Ambient ATLAS provenance is Model/Data.lean and
KernelEquations/source/README.md. Every used assertion requires a Lean proof.
-/

